Current limits are:

Per request: resolvePendingPathRequest calls A* with a hard cap of kPathNodeBudget = 512 nodes each time we pop a pending path (see src/Game.cpp:565).
Per frame time budget: The path queue is processed until it has spent PathBudgetMs = 3.0 milliseconds of CPU time in that frame (include/Game.h:674, src/Game.cpp:563-577). Once either the node budget is exhausted or the 3 ms window is hit, the loop stops and any unfinished job is requeued.
So each unit’s A* search gets at most 512 node expansions per attempt, and the whole pathfinding system is capped at ~3 ms of work per frame.

