Each “node” in that 512 limit is just one tile that A* expands while it searches. On a 128×128 map you’ve got 16 k tiles total, so 512 nodes is a fairly shallow search—enough for short paths, but long detours or clogged routes eat the budget quickly and get deferred to the next frame.

Your timing log shows the entire pathfinding pass averaging 0.17 ms and peaking under 0.5 ms, with 3 ms of frame budget reserved. That means we’re barely touching the allowance: the queue exits because it has processed all requests, not because it hit the time cap.

